_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00069"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Signature of LogWarn","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00066"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Signature of WithLevel","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00131"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"PlatformDesign","id":"SNIP_ADAPTIVE_CAN_FIGURE_Figure_16_1","is_figure":true,"page":74,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_LOG_00204"],"text":"Figure 16.1: Overview Log and Trace The ara::log Functional Cluster defines a \"Builder\"-pattern inspired set of APIs for constructing non-modeled messages and a single member function ara::log::Logger::Log for sending modeled messages. Unlike the non-modeled message APIs, it represents a single-call interface, i.e. a single function call passes all arguments to the Logger instance and performs all necessary actions to generate and send the message. This has the advantage that the runtime cost for a modeled message that is eventually not being output (because the messages log level does not reach the configured log level threshold) can be made very small: after parameter passing and function call, a single if clause checks the log level threshold and immediately returns if the threshold is not reached. This contrasts with the non-modeled message APIs, where multiple function calls are performed for constructing a message object, even if that is then eventually discarded.","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger Log function for modeled messages","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00204"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"EXP_SWArchitecture","id":"SNIP_ADAPTIVE_CAN_FIGURE_Figure_9_15","is_figure":true,"page":57,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_LOG_00068","SWS_LOG_00065","SWS_LOG_00064","SWS_LOG_00067","SWS_LOG_00069","SWS_LOG_00066"],"text":"Figure 9.15: Interfaces of Log and Trace Name: Logger Technology: Native interface Usage: Public API Description: This interface represents a logger context. The logging framework defines contexts which can be seen as logger instances within one application process or process scope. A context will be automatically registered against the Logging back-end during creation phase, as well as automatically de-registered during process shutdown phase. IsEnabled Check if the provided log level is enabled in the current configured log level. Log Logs a message modeled in the Manifest. LogDebug Creates a LogStream object with Debug severity . LogError Creates a LogStream object with Error severity . LogFatal Creates a LogStream object with Fatal severity . LogInfo Creates a LogStream object with Info severity . LogVerbose Creates a LogStream object with Verbose severity . LogWarn Creates a LogStream object with Warn severity . Operations: WithLevel Creates a LogStream object with the provided log level. Name: LogOperations Technology: Native interface Usage: Public API Description: This interface provides access to the logging framework and utility operations to control the format of value printed to the log output. ▽","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogDebug method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00068"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogError method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00065"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogFatal method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00064"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogInfo method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00067"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogVerbose method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00069"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogWarn method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00066"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"EXP_SWArchitecture","id":"SNIP_ADAPTIVE_CAN_FIGURE_Figure_9_16","is_figure":true,"page":59,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_LOG_00068","SWS_LOG_00065"],"text":"Figure 9.16: Interfaces of Log and Trace Name: Logger Technology: Native interface Usage: Public API Description: This interface represents a logger context. The logging framework defines contexts which can be seen as logger instances within one application process or process scope. A context will be automatically registered against the Logging back-end during creation phase, as well as automatically de-registered during process shutdown phase. IsEnabled Check if the provided log level is enabled in the current configured log level. Log Logs a message modeled in the Manifest. LogDebug Creates a LogStream object with Debug severity . Operations: LogError Creates a LogStream object with Error severity . ▽","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogDebug method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00068"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogError method","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_LOG_00065"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","id":"FIG-08f92a380f91aec1","is_figure":true,"page":141,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_LOG_00068","SWS_LOG_00065","SWS_LOG_00064","SWS_LOG_00067","SWS_LOG_00069","SWS_LOG_00066"],"text":"Figure 9.78: Interfaces required by Update and Configuration Management (part 2)","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Logger LogDebug method signature","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION